I am very poor and needy;
I am wounded in my heart.
My life passes like a shadow,
Like a locust shaken off.
Both my knees are weak from fasting;
Gaunt my body has become.
I am scorned by my accusers;
Seeing me, they shake their heads.

The nations He will judge,
Their dead will fill the land;
In many lands He’ll strike
Their rulers in command.
He will drink from the waterside;
Victorious, lift His head on high.

He helps the poor with generosity;
His good endures, his horn is lifted high.
The wicked sees and grinds his teeth in rage;
But he will vanish, his lust will perish.

When it saw, the sea fled quickly, 
River Jordan made retreat; 
Mountains then like rams were leaping; 
Hills were skipping just like lambs.

Though they have ears, they cannot hear;
Their nose no scent has found.
Their hands can’t feel, their feet can’t walk;
Their throats can make no sound.

Upon the LORD’s name then I called,
In my extremity:
“O LORD, I beg You, spare my life;
And let my soul go free.”
The LORD our God is kind and just;
Compassionate is He.
The LORD preserves the meek in heart;
From depths He rescued me.

Our God, the Lord, is merciful and righteous;
Gracious, the Lord preserves the simple ones.
When I was low, to me He gave salvation.
Turn back again, my soul, and be at rest;
Rest, for the LORD has dealt well with you.
My helpless soul You have delivered from death.

I’ll bring to You an off’ring of thanksgiving;
With sacrifice I’ll call upon the Lord.
I’ll pay the LORD the vows which I have promised;
This I will do where all His people meet,
Within His courts, the house of the Lord,
Within your midst, Jerusalem. Praise the Lord!

Praise the LORD! Praise the LORD!
All you nations, extol Him; 
Extol Him, all you peoples;
For great is His love toward us,
And the faithfulness of the LORD
Endures forever.

I will not pass away in death;
No, I will surely live;
And to the works the LORD has done 
My testimony give.
The LORD severely chastened me,
And stern correction gave;
But He withheld the stroke of death,
And spared me from the grave.

You are my God, I’ll give You thanks;
My God, I’ll give you praise.
O thank the LORD, for He is good;
His love lasts endless days.

My soul clings to the dust - revive;
And as You promised, let it be. 
When I recount my ways, You hear;
Your ordinances teach to me.

I’ll ponder all Your wondrous works;
And Your commands O help me see.
My soul is shedding tears of grief;
As You have promised, strengthen me.

A life of falsehood take from me;
Your law now give me in Your grace.
I chose the life of faithfulness;
Before me I Your judgments place.

LORD, let me not be put to shame;
Your testimonies I hold fast.
I’ll run the way of Your commands;
My mind You will enlarge at last.

O take away my feared disgrace;
Your laws are good indeed.
Revive me in Your righteousness;
I long for Your decrees.

The proud have smeared me with their lies;
Your precepts are my choice.
Their hearts, enclosed in fat, are dull;
I in Your law rejoice.

My soul is fainting to see Your salvation;
Yet do I put all my hope in Your word.
My eyes grow dim as I look for Your promise;
When will you give me Your comfort deferred?

People of double mind I hate;
Your law my love has stirred.
You are my shield and hiding place;
My hope is in Your word.

