In Babylon we thought of Zion;
Sitting beside the streams, we wept.
We hung our harps upon the willows.
By cruel men as captives kept;
They called for mirth and singing thus:
“Sing one of Zion’s songs for us.”

All kings of earth will thank You, LORD;
They’ll sing when they have heard Your word.
The LORD’s ways they will celebrate;
The glory of the LORD is great.

