I call You, LORD, make haste to me; 
When You I call, O hear my plea.
And let my prayer as incense rise; 
Raised hands as evening’s sacrifice.

Restrain my mouth, LORD, my lips guard;
From all that’s evil, keep my heart,
From deeds with those who work deceit;
Let me not from their banquet eat.

And so to You, O Sovereign LORD,
I look with longing eyes;
Do not leave me defenseless now;
On You my soul relies.
O keep me from the traps and snares
That wicked men have set.
While I pass safely, let them fall;
Catch them in their own net.

Yet I recall the past;
I muse on all Your deeds;
I think of all Your hands have done.
I stretch my hands to You;
My soul longs after You
As thirsts a dry and desert land.

O LORD, deliver me
From all my enemies;
Teach me Your will, I hide in You 
You truly are my God;
May Your good Spirit lead,
Directing me on level ground.

His mercies cover all He’s made;
Good is the LORD to all who live.
All of Your works will praise You, LORD;
Your saints to You will praises give.

The eyes of all are turned to You;
Their food in season You will give;
You satisfy with opened hand
Desires of everything that lives.

The LORD is just in all His ways;
In all His works His love is shown;
The LORD is near to all who call,
Who call in truth on Him alone.

I will extol You, my God and Sov’reign, 
And I will give Your name endless praise. 
Day after day my praise I will give You; 
I will exalt Your name evermore. 
Great is the LORD, most worthy of praises;
His greatness none can fully discern.

Those humbled low the LORD will raise;
He casts the wicked down.
O praise the LORD our God with thanks;
With harp His praises sound.
